  provenance: "PROVISIONAL L1 SEMANTIC LAYER - not a final claim about the specimen.\n\nFeature
    identity (L1 declaration):\n  Both long edge polylines -> SharpEdge.\n  Blade
    flats, bevels and centreline -> non-cutting.\n  Guard, grip, pommel and markers
    are not represented here at all; they collide via the\n  compound colliders and
    are never contact bearing.\n\nEdge basis: the existing PhysicalQuillon convention,
    via StartStateProbe.CrossSection.\n  edge = quillon direction orthogonalised
    to the blade axis; face = cross(axis, edge).\n  No new convention or frame is
    introduced; GeometricExtents is NOT used as a fallback.\n  Computed from the
    specimen's own quillon and tip markers rather than the station's\n  SwordRef_*/Q1,Q2,Tip
    reference targets, so the runtime path needs no BindMetrics and no\n  station
    object. Those are the same three physical features, so the convention is identical.\n 
    The station tools remain the alignment and observability oracle.\n\n  bladeAxis
    (local) = (-0.999767, 0.021566, 0.000000)\n  edgeAxis  (local) = (0.000000, 0.000000,
    1.000000)   (+edge; the opposite long edge is -this)\n  faceNormal(local) = (0.021566,
    0.999767, 0.000000)\n\nSign note: BOTH long edges are designated SharpEdge for
    L1, so L1 classification is\ninvariant to the sign of edgeAxis. The sign is recorded
    for orientation comparison against\nshowEdgePairClosest / showEdgeContainment,
    not because L1 depends on it.\n\nMeasured geometry (observation, NOT the sharpness
    rule): included angle at the designated\n  edges is 25.00 degrees, computed by
    the builder from the authored facets.\n  Whether that counts as sharp is a separate
    declared criterion and is not encoded here.\n\nBuilt from Assets/P3T/Prefabs/V2_SW_A1_MeshOnly.prefab
    -> Blade (ProBuilder), 5 authored stations,\ntessellated at 0.01 m -> 2492 surfaces,
    1236 edge\nlines, of which 206 are designated sharp."
